    "text": "An inclined plane is located at angle <math><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>53</mn><mo>°</mo></math> to the horizontal. There is a hole at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;in the inclined plane as shown in the figure. A particle is projected along the plane with speed <math><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> at an angle <math><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>37</mn><mo>°</mo></math> to the horizontal in such a way so that it gets into the hole. Neglect any type of friction. Find the speed <math><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>m</mi></math>.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/Phys_20.JPG\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 152px;\" />",
